{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789068478,"nonce":"5g+o1FwN/VIt6j95SRdK0kP6+mw=","message":"The eleven functions, and a fix that did NOT work.\n\nASH_FIBER_REPORT=names (added for this) gives the suspend set by name. Diffing the hosting build against the non-hosting one, these eleven join it:\n\n    qsort  __qsort_r  sift  trinkle  wrapper_cmp\n    hlp_alloc_dynamic  hlp_type_array  hlp_type_bytes\n    hlp_type_dyn  hlp_type_f64  hlp_type_i32\n\nThey are exactly the functions the linker exports for a side module, which is why the set grows only when a library sits beside the program. Two of them line up with the symptom uncomfortably well: hlp_alloc_dynamic allocates a boxed dynamic and hlp_type_f64 supplies the HF64 type, and the value found in the closure slot is a boxed dynamic of type HF64.\n\n**The fix that followed from that was wrong.** Reasoning: a side module never passes through the transform, so its frames carry no ladder; instrumenting a function it calls puts a suspend point under a caller that cannot honour one. Making those eleven barriers reduced the instrumented set from 2642 to 2635 (2631 without a library) -- and the failure survived, 1 run in 150, with the identical signature (kind=6, fun_ptr=0, same static HF64 type address). Reverted in 51d0b33.\n\nIt is worth saying why it is reverted rather than kept as harmless. qsort takes a COMPARATOR, and a Haxe comparator is Haxe code that may legitimately need to suspend. Making qsort a barrier stops the closure there, so a fiber suspending inside a comparator would unwind through an uninstrumented qsort frame -- trading a hypothesis for a real breakage. If this line is picked up again, the shape that could work is two entry points (one suspendable for the program, one not for the library), not a blanket barrier.\n\nSo the side-module dependency is established and its mechanism is still unexplained. What is now known and should not be re-derived:\n\n- the value is a boxed HF64 dynamic, not corrupted memory (instrumented guard, e91b33f)\n- the suspend set differs by exactly those eleven names\n- refused and unsavable are 0 in both builds, so nothing is being declined\n- the fiber save area IS a GC root, and its bounds ARE checked\n- ASH_GC_STRESS: 0 of 60 against 1 of 60, so not a rooting bug\n- rate: about 1 in 60 to 1 in 150 direct, 3 of 8 CI runs","files":null}]}